Type the EVO scan-lock state slot with NVEvoLockAction

NVEvoSubDevRec.scanLockState takes NvU32 action, while every lock state function
in g_nvkms-evo-states.c takes NVEvoLockAction. C accepts the 183 assignments
because the enum is compatible with its underlying integer type; kCFI hashes the
two apart, so each modeset traps in nvEvoLockStatePreModeset/PostModeset. The enum
moves from nvkms-evo-states.h, which includes nvkms-types.h, to nvkms-types.h so
that the slot can name it.

